<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106792" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπᾰγορ-εύω</span></b> , the aor. being in 
			Att.
		 (but not in later Gr., cf. <i><span class="en">
			J.
			<u>AJ</u>
			3.5.3
		</span></i>, etc.) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεῖπον</span> (q.v.),
			pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείρηκα</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dictate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				15.7
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				17
			</span></i>; freq. in Pap., <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				592 ii 4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράψαι τὸ ὑπαγορευθέν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Top.</u>
					142b32
				</span></i>
			: more generally, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃ δεῖ ποιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					17.29
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὑπαγορευομένη διάθεσις</span>
			the <i>given</i> state of health, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i> Trall.<i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>suggest,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπίδα, πρόφασιν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.2.32
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				39
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Marcellin.
				<u>Puls.</u>
				172
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.314
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Posidon.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				6.2
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυσίας καὶ καθαρμούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Marc.</u>
					29
				</span></i>
			: folld. by inf., <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Th.</u>
				19
			</span></i>:—impers. in 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Epict.
				<u>Ench.</u>
				30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>imply, indicate without the use of a special word</i> or
				<i>form,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξὺν νηῒ . . ὑπαγορεύει ξὺν μιᾷ νηΐ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					72.17
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				278.12
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			), al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>reply,</i>
			
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιβληθέντος</span>
			 in Dinarchus, <i><span class="en">Harp.,
					<u>AB</u>409</span></i> (
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			<i>enumerate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anon.Lond.
				11.42
			</span></i>; <i>name, call by a title,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῷ "περὶ μετοχῆσ" ὑπηγορευμένῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					302.10
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				337.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῦτα φρενιτικὰ εἶναι ὑπαγόρευε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.Med.
				</span></i>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				58.71
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
